<title>FRANCE: Radar keeps French barges at snail's pace.</title>
<headline>Radar keeps French barges at snail's pace.</headline>
<dateline>LILLE, France 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>French canal police are carrying out radar checks to spot barges breaking the speed limit -- of eight kph (five mph).</p>
<p>Police said the first checks, in the north of the country, had established that most barges were speeding, sailing at up to 12 kph (seven mph). Experts say speeding barges cause water swirls that damage canal banks.</p>
